Advanced relativistic fields, action and conservation (@em-relativity-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1", #source "../sources/Electromagnetic-Theory-MIT-8-311.lingua#r_76PF2M392RCSAEEF88YX03ZEBH", #source "../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H", #electromagnetism "../study/An-integrated-electromagnetic-system-investigation.lingua#r_1FQW2ASX2WCT3JRXKKP4NB4HSN") { r_1PN7ASKXD515XZCY9T1FDPJCP5
**Read:** [Electromagnetism — David Tong](../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1), complete relativity, covariant and action sections; [Electromagnetic Theory — MIT 8.311, Spring 2004](../sources/Electromagnetic-Theory-MIT-8-311.lingua#r_76PF2M392RCSAEEF88YX03ZEBH), full applicable graduate course work; [Classical Electromagnetism — Richard Fitzpatrick](../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H), complete relativistic electrodynamics chapters.

Work the full relativity/covariant-field/action treatment in [Electromagnetism — David Tong](../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1), the corresponding [Classical Electromagnetism — Richard Fitzpatrick](../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H) chapters and the complete relevant [Electromagnetic Theory — MIT 8.311, Spring 2004](../sources/Electromagnetic-Theory-MIT-8-311.lingua#r_76PF2M392RCSAEEF88YX03ZEBH) lecture/problem sequence. Reconstruct Lorentz transformations, four-current conservation, tensor field equations and the vacuum energy-momentum tensor with one declared metric and SI convention.

Choose a moving charge/current distribution or crossed-field particle problem. Solve it in two inertial frames, transform sources, simultaneity, fields, particle motion and energy/momentum, and compare the same physical observable. Verify both field invariants and the ordinary component Maxwell equations. An algebraic tensor identity alone is not enough; the source geometry and boundary conditions must be transformed too.

Derive the action variation and explain gauge invariance and source work for the chosen complete system. Compare at least two textbook sign/unit conventions by explicit conversion. Extend the problem until a quasistatic approximation breaks down or radiation becomes relevant, and identify the needed extra treatment. Present enough intermediate reasoning for a reader to distinguish a physical contradiction from a coordinate, normalization or simultaneity error. This study supplies graduate classical depth without pretending to finish quantum field theory or gravitation.

**Continue:** [An integrated electromagnetic-system investigation](../study/An-integrated-electromagnetic-system-investigation.lingua#r_1FQW2ASX2WCT3JRXKKP4NB4HSN).

**Return:** [Electromagnetism — charge, fields, matter, waves and physical evidence](../Electromagnetism.lingua#r_5TJPESCTTNAKY66JH2QNQYN1PY).
